            <ArticleTitle>[Pharmaco-ethological study of analgesia induced by intraspecies fighting behavior].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>690-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The time-dependent characteristics and ethological features of intraspecies fighting-induced analgesia were demonstrated in experiments on dominant and submissive-defeated mice. Opiate but not GABAergic mechanisms were found to be involved in fighting-induced analgesia in submissive-defeated mice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
